{"variants":[{"paths":["\/documentation\/miamidiagrams\/miamistatemachine\/statemachine\/mermaiddiagram"],"traits":[{"interfaceLanguage":"swift"}]}],"kind":"symbol","primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["macOS"],"tokens":[{"text":"nonisolated","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mermaidDiagram","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"text":"String","preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" { ","kind":"text"},{"text":"get","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" }","kind":"text"}]}]},{"kind":"content","content":[{"type":"heading","anchor":"discussion","level":2,"text":"Discussion"},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"Every state is declared with its description, and with an identifier","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"made up from its position among the states, like ","type":"text"},{"code":"state1","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":". A description","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"can be any text, which an identifier in Mermaid cannot. The states","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"connected by transitions are connected by an arrow, labeled with the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"events. If several events lead from a state to the same state, they","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"share one arrow. The initial state has an arrow leading to it from the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"start, written ","type":"text"},{"code":"[*]","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and every ending state has an arrow to the end.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"text":"The diagram is the same every time, whatever order the transitions were","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"given in, so it can be compared with a saved diagram. This needs the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"states to have different descriptions. States with the same description","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"are still different states in the diagram, but which of them that gets","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"which identifier can differ.","type":"text"}]},{"type":"aside","content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":"), where "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"text":"n","type":"text"}]},{"type":"text","text":" is the number of transitions."}]}],"name":"Complexity","style":"note"}]}],"schemaVersion":{"minor":3,"major":0,"patch":0},"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The definition of the state machine as a diagram, in the language of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Mermaid. It is drawn where Mermaid is, like in Markdown on GitHub, when"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"put in a code block marked "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"mermaid"},{"type":"text","text":"."}],"metadata":{"role":"symbol","roleHeading":"Instance Property","fragments":[{"text":"var","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"mermaidDiagram","kind":"identifier"},{"text":": ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:SS","text":"String","kind":"typeIdentifier"}],"symbolKind":"property","externalID":"s:17MiamiStateMachine0bC0C0A8DiagramsE14mermaidDiagramSSvp","modules":[{"name":"MiamiDiagrams","relatedModules":["MiamiStateMachine"]}],"extendedModule":"MiamiStateMachine","conformance":{"availabilityPrefix":[{"text":"Available when","type":"text"}],"conformancePrefix":[{"text":"Conforms when","type":"text"}],"constraints":[{"code":"Event","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" conforms to ","type":"text"},{"code":"StateMachineEvent","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", ","type":"text"},{"code":"State","type":"